---
import PolicyLayout from "../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro";
import { business } from "../siteConstants/business";
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How personal data is collected, used and protected under Malaysia's Personal Data Protection Act 2010 (PDPA)."
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy is issued by {business.name} ({business.ssmNo}) ("we",
    "us"), the data user, under the Personal Data Protection Act 2010 (PDPA). It
    explains what personal data we collect, why we collect it, who we share it
    with and how you can access or correct it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Personal data we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Identity and contact details:</strong> name, email address, phone
      number, company name and billing address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Project information:</strong> requirements, content, files and
      account access you provide so we can deliver the work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payment information:</strong> payments are processed by CHIP. We
      receive the transaction reference, amount, status and payment method
      type. We do not receive or store your full card number, CVV or online
      banking credentials.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Communications:</strong> emails, messages and meeting notes
      exchanged with us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data:</strong> standard server logs kept by our hosting
      provider, such as IP address, browser type and pages visited.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Purposes of processing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to enquiries and prepare quotations.</li>
    <li>To deliver, support and maintain the services you engage us for.</li>
    <li>To issue invoices, collect payments and process refunds.</li>
    <li>To keep business, accounting and tax records required by law.</li>
    <li>To keep our website and systems secure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. PDPA principles and how we apply them</h2>

  <h3>General Principle</h3>
  <p>
    We process personal data only with your consent, or where it is necessary
    to perform a contract with you, to comply with a legal obligation, or as
    otherwise permitted by the PDPA. We only collect data that is adequate,
    relevant and not excessive for the purposes above.
  </p>

  <h3>Notice and Choice Principle</h3>
  <p>
    This policy is our written notice to you. Providing contact and billing
    details is necessary for us to quote, deliver and invoice; if you choose
    not to provide them, we may be unable to provide our services. You may
    withdraw consent to further processing at any time by contacting us, subject
    to any legal or contractual obligations we have.
  </p>

  <h3>Disclosure Principle</h3>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data. We disclose it only for the purposes
    above, and only to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>CHIP (chip-in.asia)</strong>, our payment processor, and the
      banks, card networks and e-wallet providers it works with, to process
      payments and refunds;
    </li>
    <li>
      hosting, email, cloud storage and code-hosting providers we use to run
      our website and deliver projects (for example Google Firebase Hosting
      and GitHub);
    </li>
    <li>accountants, auditors and professional advisers;</li>
    <li>
      government agencies, regulators or courts where required by law.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers may store data outside Malaysia. Where that happens
    we take reasonable steps to ensure your data receives a comparable level of
    protection.
  </p>

  <h3>Security Principle</h3>
  <p>
    We take practical steps to protect personal data from loss, misuse,
    modification, unauthorised access and disclosure. These include encrypted
    connections (HTTPS), access controls and multi-factor authentication on our
    accounts, and limiting access to people who need it.
  </p>

  <h3>Retention Principle</h3>
  <p>
    We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes above.
    Invoices, payment and accounting records are kept for at least 7 years to
    meet Malaysian tax and company record-keeping requirements. Other project
    data is deleted or anonymised once it is no longer needed.
  </p>

  <h3>Data Integrity Principle</h3>
  <p>
    We take reasonable steps to keep personal data accurate, complete, not
    misleading and up to date. Please tell us if any of your details change.
  </p>

  <h3>Access Principle</h3>
  <p>
    You have the right to request access to, and correction of, the personal
    data we hold about you. Send your request in writing using the contact
    details below. We will respond within 21 days of receiving it, as required
    by the PDPA. We may need to verify your identity first, and may refuse a
    request where the PDPA allows us to.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising or analytics cookies. Our hosting
    provider may set technical cookies or keep logs needed to serve the site
    securely.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version is always
    on this page, with the date it was last updated.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact for access, correction and enquiries</h2>
  <p>
    {business.name}<br />
    {business.address}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a><br />
    Phone: {business.phone}
  </p>
  <p>
    If this policy is ever translated, the English version prevails. A Bahasa
    Malaysia version is available on request.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
